# 🔮 Madame Zara — Oracle of Fates

**Live Site:** [https://kmorgan37.github.io/Mini-Project-2/fortune-teller/](https://kmorgan37.github.io/Mini-Project-2/fortune-teller/)

## What It Does

Madame Zara is a fortune teller web app where you consult an all-knowing oracle for dramatic, mysterious readings. Enter your name, choose a category — Love, Career, Destiny, Warnings, or Pure Chaos — and click the glowing crystal ball to receive your fate. Fortunes reveal themselves with a typewriter animation, and every consultation is logged in your session history.

## Inspiration

In my junior year of high school, my AP Psychology teacher was Ms. Zara. She had a genuine fascination with fortune telling and would weave it into lessons about perception, bias, and the human need to find meaning. She made it feel less like superstition and more like a window into how people think. When I needed a name for my oracle, there was really only one choice.

## How to Use

1. Type your name in the first field
2. Select a category from the dropdown (Love, Career, Destiny, Warnings, or Chaos)
3. Click the crystal ball — or press Enter — to receive your fortune
4. Consult as many times as you like; your session history tracks every reading
5. Hit **Clear All & Begin Again** to reset everything and start fresh

## Features

- 5 fortune categories with 10 unique fortunes each (50 total)
- Typewriter animation reveals your fortune letter by letter
- Glowing crystal ball with shake and swirling mist effects
- Session history log with consultation counter
- Full reset without page refresh
- Works on mobile and desktop
- Keyboard accessible (Enter key triggers the oracle)

## What I Learned

- How to use JavaScript Promises and async/await to sequence animations
- How to manipulate the DOM dynamically to build and update a history list
- How to handle user input validation and give visual feedback on errors
- How to create atmospheric CSS effects using gradients, animations, and box-shadow
- The importance of planning state variables before writing any logic